  "id": "COMPOUND:33673 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Petroraspailyne B1 and CCF-STTG1 through a series of target interactions. Petroraspailyne B1 is implicated in targeting Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is a key enzyme involved in epigenetic regulation. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 24-Methylenecycloartanone, both of which have been shown to interact with CCF-STTG1. These findings collectively indicate that Petroraspailyne B1 may act as a modulator of the epigenetic pathway, influencing the activity of CCF-STTG1 through the regulation of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Petroraspailyne B1 and CCF-STTG1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
